# Fingerprints of findings gitleaks reports that are NOT secrets.
#
# One fingerprint per line, in the form printed by gitleaks when it blocks:
#   <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>
# For a finding in the working tree (gitleaks protect) the commit part is empty.
#
# Every entry needs a comment saying why it is not a secret and who decided that.
# An unexplained fingerprint is an unreviewed leak.
#
# This repo's history scanned clean when the gate was installed, so the file starts empty.
